⚖️ Saga vs 2PC (Two-Phase Commit)
| Feature          | Saga Pattern              | 2PC                          |
| ---------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Type             | Eventually consistent     | Strongly consistent          |
| Performance      | ✅ Fast, scalable          | ❌ Slower, blocking           |
| Coordination     | App-level                 | XA transaction manager       |
| Rollback         | Manual compensation logic | Automatic rollback           |
| Failure handling | Compensating transactions | Retry or failure propagation |


✅ Pros of Saga Pattern
Works well with microservices

No global lock or coordinator

Scalable and asynchronous

Good for long-running transactions

❌ Challenges
Compensating actions can be complex

More effort to handle failure scenarios

Debugging is harder due to async nature

Requires idempotency and retry logic

