@KafkaListener(topics = "order-topic", groupId = "saga")
public void handleSagaResponse(String event) {
    if (event.contains("FAILED")) {
        System.out.println("Compensating: Canceling order...");
        // rollback: maybe update status to CANCELED in DB
    } else if (event.contains("COMPLETED")) {
        System.out.println("Order completed successfully!");
    }
}
✅ Summary
Each microservice reacts to events (Choreography).

No central coordinator.

Rollbacks are handled using compensation events.

🔐 Key Considerations
Idempotency is critical in case of retries.

Use transactional Kafka if needed for reliability.

Add timeouts and retry handling for real-world scenarios.



